From bd6e1d896485e807ad30fe8a194c3d6b153e9278 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:59:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] moal: do not copy every transmitted skb by default

tx_skb_clone defaulted to 1 on every platform, which sets
EXT_TX_SKB_CLONE and makes woal_start_xmit() take
skb_realloc_headroom() unconditionally. With enough headroom already
present that call is pskb_copy(): a new skb and a full copy of the frame,
then a free of the original, for every packet, on the single TX worker.
On the 88W9098 that worker is the throughput ceiling, and a profile of a
wire-to-Wi-Fi transfer showed the copy and the free as the two largest
items on it.

The predicate the flag bypasses already handles the case it was added
for -- a cloned skb, or one short of the TxPD headroom, is still copied.
Default to 0; the parameter remains for platforms that want the copy.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 mlinux/moal_init.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mlinux/moal_init.c b/mlinux/moal_init.c
index 5e1bfb1..e96e067 100644
--- a/mlinux/moal_init.c
+++ b/mlinux/moal_init.c
@@ -208,7 +208,13 @@ static int rps = 0x0F;
  * Default value of 0 keeps edmac disabled by default
  */
 static int edmac_ctrl = 0;
-static int tx_skb_clone = 1;
+/* Off: woal_start_xmit() already copies an skb that is cloned or short of
+ * headroom, which is the case this flag was added for. Set, it forces a
+ * full copy of every transmitted frame (skb_realloc_headroom on an skb with
+ * enough headroom is pskb_copy), which on a single-threaded TX worker is
+ * the largest per-packet cost in the driver.
+ */
+static int tx_skb_clone = 0;
 
 #ifdef IMX_SUPPORT
 static int pmqos = 1;
